From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:12:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/38] Style lists, swipe rows and turn hit testing off on
 Linux

A list is inset grouped by default, as on iOS, or grouped or plain by
listStyle; rows outside a section share a card, with separators between
rows. listRowBackground, listRowSeparator, listRowInsets and
scrollContentBackground work, List takes data, and a list row shows its
swipeActions on a sideways drag, onDelete adding a Delete one.
allowsHitTesting(false) keeps touches from a view and what it contains.

A whole list row is its NavigationLink. A button's pressed state no longer
holds the touch once the finger moves, so rows and scroll views around
buttons get their drags. The stdout app lays out at the scale of the
frames it draws, so hairlines stay, and gets a swipe command.
